Implemented under `/output` as ESM `.mjs` modules and verified against the provided executable for sampled help text, parse errors, and URL rewrite cases.

Library files:
- [path-utils.mjs](/output/lib/path-utils.mjs)
- [cli.mjs](/output/lib/cli.mjs)
- [urlish.mjs](/output/lib/urlish.mjs)
- [app.mjs](/output/lib/app.mjs)

Entry file:
- [test2.mjs](/output/test2.mjs)

`test2.mjs`:
```js
import { main } from "./lib/app.mjs";

export { main } from "./lib/app.mjs";

const exitCode = main();
if (exitCode !== 0) {
  process.exitCode = exitCode;
}
```

Sample run parity was checked with cases like `--help`, missing required args, unknown args, `http://...`, `//...`, `mailto:...`, empty host, credentials, and ports. Runtime invalid-host failures use the same validation message, with Node-native stack formatting.
